 (10,'DEF-001','V2 reaction wake','deferred','done','P2','G8','FS-004','V2','specs/gameplay-algorithms.md (V2)',NULL,'Deferred. Re-checked 16 Sep after the capacity runs: the wake-scheduling mechanism already exists (SessionDecisionService::scheduleSuccessor accepts an absolute next_due_at) and the inbound ETA is already observed (PerceptionSnapshot::inboundFleets[].time_arrival), so V2 no longer depends on full SP3. It stays deferred because the reaction-window semantics rework the shipped save-on-notice behaviour (V1): withhold when arrival > 180 s out, schedule a wake at arrival - draw(120,180), save inside the window, never save below the host 10 s detector floor - and that touches V3 (SaveFailurePolicy draw timing), V6 (proactive absence saves) and the dark-period wake logic. Needs a live inbound-fleet re-measure to calibrate the window boundary first. Narrow path: publish reaction_wake_at in inboundThreat(), clamp next_due_at in SessionDecisionService, re-base fleetsave tests on the window.','2026-09-16 19:11:25'),
