 (108,'LLM-010','S9 — settle the provider cache-read tokens (cost undercount)','impl','done','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'specs/llm-full-utilisation.md (S9)','app/Infrastructure/Language/LaravelAiLanguageGateway.php; app/Actions/SettleAiUsageReservationAction.php; app/Models/AiUsageReservation.php; app/Actions/BuildAiPilotReportAction.php; app/Actions/SummarizeAiOperabilityAction.php','DISC-008 output. The SDK Usage exposes cacheReadInputTokens and both parsers subtract it from promptTokens (DeepSeek ParsesTextResponses.php:86; OpenAI :142-148), but LaravelAiLanguageGateway reads promptTokens/completionTokens only and SettleAiUsageReservationAction passes a hardcoded 0 into the cached parameter ResolveAiUsageCostAction already prices. So cached input is invisible: uncounted, never charged at the cached_input rate in config/pricing.php, and no lane reports a cache-hit rate. Carry the value through the existing settle path, store it, count it in the input ceiling (promptTokens + cached), report hits per provider/model. Cache-write tokens stay unplumbed (neither supported provider bills them). Spec: plan/details/specs/llm-full-utilisation.md S9.','2026-09-17 18:11:38'),
 (109,'PVE-001','Campaign momentum: the faction races the same objective (7E instance)','deferred','deferred','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'specs/pve-empire.md','app/Models/AiCampaign.php; app/Actions/AdvanceAiCampaignStateAction.php; app/Actions/DeclareAiCampaignObjectiveAction.php','DISC-009 output, research idea 1+2+3 folded. Today an Active campaign resolves only on completion and fails on the deadline; the faction advances nothing, so time is the only opponent. Add one counter on AiCampaign plus the faction''s own declared objective set, advanced by the existing ai:advance-campaigns pass on a published schedule, so the coalition win condition becomes complete the ladder first. Objective ordering (scout -> weaken -> final stronghold) is the escalation ladder and the same counter is the influence bar gating the decisive objective - one number, not two mechanisms. Rewards unchanged (ordinary loot/debris + verified contribution record, paid on completion). Gated by the Package 7 evidence rule: needs a campaign review record naming the gap. Spec: plan/details/specs/pve-empire.md.','2026-09-17 12:24:30'),
 (110,'PVE-002','Coalition campaign page: progress + both sides'' losses (situation log)','deferred','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'specs/pve-empire.md','resources/views/; routes/web.php','DISC-009 output, research idea 9. The spec''s deliverable list includes a module-owned coalition-facing campaign page and none exists (only the operator page at admin/ai). Content is decided by the research: objective progress and both sides'' losses as counters aggregated at write time, matching the review loop cheap-to-read rule. Deferred until a disclosed coalition campaign exists - a page for a coalition that does not exist is speculative UI. Spec: plan/details/specs/pve-empire.md.','2026-09-17 12:24:30'),
 (111,'P7-001','7A scope: ordinary-universe consultation (war declaration + new colony triggers)','deferred','deferred','P2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/WORK-PACKAGES.md (Package 7)','app/Actions/RequestCampaignConsultationAction.php; app/Enums/AiCampaignConsultationTrigger.php; app/Actions/BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction.php; config/campaign-consultation.php','Package 7A, audited 17 Sep 2026. The consultation machinery is NOT missing: transport, off/observe/advice admission, staff switch, trigger allowlist, cooldown, concurrency cap, daily ceilings, receipts, deterministic validation, profile-bounded ranking nudge, thinking-model routing and read-only tools all ship (6A/6B/6C + S4/S5/S8). Six triggers already fire: FleetLoss, RepeatedSetback, ContestedObjective, CoalitionConflict, NewPhase, RankChange. What is genuinely left: (a) two unbuilt events - worth adding only when a caller exists: war declaration and new colony; (b) the shipped lane is campaign-keyed - RequestCampaignConsultationAction::handle() takes an AiCampaign and BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction builds from it - so ordinary-universe (non-campaign) advice is a shape change, not a config flag, and needs its own budget, caps and evidence gate. Gate: a review record naming a player-visible gap (Package 7 rule).','2026-09-17 12:43:58'),
 (112,'P7-002','7B: semantic recall only if a held-out review beats native retrieval','deferred','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/WORK-PACKAGES.md (Package 7)','app/Infrastructure/Memory/AgentOsLongTermMemory.php; app/Domain/Memory/LongTermMemorySelector.php; app/Actions/EvaluateAiSocialExchangeAction.php','Package 7B, audited 17 Sep 2026. Gate: a held-out review showing native retrieval misses what exact/entity recall closes. The starting evidence points the other way. The AgentOS recall benchmark (15 Sep 2026, 30 trials, Modules/AI/scripts/e2e-agentos-recall-benchmark.php, runs inside ogamex-app) measured the driver value as SUBSTITUTION, not addition: the +33.3pp required-fact recall IS the eviction of newest facts (newest-kept 1/30 external vs 30/30 native), with the promotion unbounded, and the sole consumer (NativeSocialCognition::outstandingDebtPenalty) is unreachable in production because every real help request answers Counter: insufficient_available_amount. Reference profile also runs no local model, so any embedder is a paid hosted call. Reopen only with a held-out review that shows a miss native retrieval cannot close.','2026-09-17 12:43:58'),
 (113,'P7-003','7C: PsychSim diplomacy experiment (driver integration + consumer)','deferred','deferred','P3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plan/WORK-PACKAGES.md (Package 7)','','Package 7C, audited 17 Sep 2026. PsychSim appears nowhere in the module (grep of app/, config/, tests/ is empty) and is not one of the four supported drivers (native + FAtiMA/CiF + CBRKit + AgentOS), so this is a driver integration plus a diplomacy consumer - the deepest dependency and the least evidenced of Package 7''s slices. Spec bound: one account and 1-3 relevant counterparts at depth one (depth two needs a recorded measured gain and capacity evidence); it may propose social stance or coalition evidence, never fleets, resources, promises or a replacement player runtime. Gate: Package 6 acceptance + a review record naming the gap.','2026-09-17 12:43:58'),
 (114,'REV-005','Confirm the wave-10 session-cost measurements (W10-1, W10-2)','review','done','P1','W10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/plan/details/GAP-REGISTER.md','Step 0 of the wave-10 performance work, and the reason neither row below may be implemented yet: reproduce the measurements on the committed build before changing code, with the read-only method recorded in the register (a DB::listen listener plus a debug_backtrace walk around one PlayerPerceptionBuilder::build, and the MySQL profiler for the server-side figure). Confirm or correct each figure: 33 queries per GameMissionFactory::getAllMissions() and 0 for the same static metadata read through a class name; ~297 of ~430 perception queries arriving from FacilityChain.php:129; ~34 PlayerService rebuilds per perception from make($id, true) across 20 module and 30 host sites; session jobs 1-36 s while sibling work kinds measure ~310 ms. Deliverable: a note under plan/details/reviews/ with the reproduced figures, the exact call sites, a verdict per row (confirmed / corrected / withdrawn), and for W10-2 the chosen mechanism plus the write-then-reread callers that were audited. No code change in this row. Corrected expectation from the 17 Sep re-measure: the mission path is 105 of 439 perception queries and 4.6-8.0 s of a 19.7-23.1 s build, not 297 queries. Also confirm the environment caveat before trusting any seconds figure: the same statement measures a 45.8 ms median through raw PDO on the application handle and 2.5 ms through the query builder in the same process, so the query counts are the portable finding and the wall clock is a property of this host.','2026-09-17 13:56:15'),
 (115,'IMPL-043','Host mission catalogue without instantiation (W10-1)','impl','done','P1','W10-1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Factories/GameMissionFactory.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php','Only after REV-005 confirms W10-1. GameMission::__construct pulls FleetMissionService and MessageService, and both constructors require a PlayerService, so resolving any mission builds a player: 4 queries for metadata that is already static (getTypeId, getRequiredResearch and getRequiredShipMachineNames are all static methods). Split the id-to-class map out of getAllMissions() into getMissionClasses(): array<int, class-string<GameMission>>; make getAllMissions() map that through resolve() so the callers that genuinely need instances keep working unchanged (FleetController plus the three admin label lists); make getMissionById() look the class up and throw a clear error for an unknown id instead of a match fallthrough. The module side is one line: FacilityChain::missionRequiredResearch() iterates the class list and calls $class::getRequiredResearch(). Acceptance: perception queries ~430 to ~130 measured on the grand universe via a restart, session jobs back in the ~300 ms band, host suite and module suite green, Gate 2 review clean. Correction 17 Sep 2026 after re-measuring: the filed figure was wrong. The catalogue is 105 of 439 perception queries and 4.6-8.0 s of a 19.7-23.1 s build (~24-36%), because the perception reaches it 3 times per build, not 9. So this row is necessary but NOT sufficient - closing it leaves ~15 s, and IMPL-045 (module-side) and IMPL-044 (host) carry the rest. Corrected acceptance: perception queries 439 -> ~334.','2026-09-17 18:11:38'),
 (116,'IMPL-044','One player reload per job (W10-2)','impl','done','P2','W10-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Factories/PlayerServiceFactory.php; app/Services/PlayerService.php','Only after REV-005 confirms W10-2. PlayerServiceFactory::make($id, true) rebuilds a PlayerService on every call (~4 queries each: users, highscores, users_tech, plus PlanetListService planets read) and one perception triggers ~34 rebuilds across 20 module and 30 host forced-reload sites. Smallest mechanism first: memoise a forced reload per generation in PlayerServiceFactory, since AppServiceProvider already flushes the singleton factories before every job (the JobProcessing listener), so a second forced reload inside one job re-reads identical rows. Alternative if the audit finds a write-then-reread caller inside one job: make the PlayerService planet list lazy instead. Risk to settle before choosing, not after: a caller that writes and then relies on a second fresh read in the same job would see stale data. Acceptance: rebuilds per perception ~34 to ~1, perception query count down again, session jobs in the ~300 ms band, host suite and module suite green.','2026-09-17 15:20:42'),
 (117,'IMPL-045','Memoise the mission research map once per worker process (W10-1)','impl','done','P1','W10-1, W10-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Perception/PlayerObservationService.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/','Shipped and deployed 17 Sep 2026: a static memo on FacilityChain, because the host mission catalogue is static and the read was repeated per chain instance (3 catalogue builds per perception). Measured on the grand universe: mission path 105 -> 39 queries, perception 439 -> 372 queries, suite 854/854 green. The player-graph half of the original row was attempted (drop make($id, true) in the 20 read sites) and reverted: it breaks AiCapabilityPublicationTest, because the factory cache is only fresh per job and a host write inside a test/request must still be visible - refiled as IMPL-046.','2026-09-17 13:46:58'),
 (118,'IMPL-046','Resolve the player once per perception instead of per call site (fresh-preserving, W10-2)','impl','done','P2','W10-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Modules/AI/app/Domain/Perception/PlayerObservationService.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/','The remaining module-side half of W10-2, after the naive version was tried and reverted: dropping make($id, true) at the 20 read sites broke AiCapabilityPublicationTest, because the factory cache is only fresh per job and a host write inside a request (or a test) must still be visible. The correct mechanism resolves the PlayerService exactly once per perception - after the session advance has already forced a reload and before any module write - and passes that instance down through PlayerObservationService and into the planners it invokes, so the read path reloads once instead of ~20 times without losing write freshness. Acceptance: the same freshness test stays green, perception queries fall from 372 toward ~300, suite green.','2026-09-17 14:43:48'),
 (119,'IMPL-047','Refuse colonising at the planet cap (live colonise-spam fix)','impl','done','P1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Domain/Decision/QueueableColonyPlanner.php','Live read 17 Sep (ogamex-grand): the old cohort (players 12-21) dispatched 4,763 colonise missions in 48h, ~2,300 of them cancelled at arrival because every account was at its host-derived planet cap (astrophysics). QueueableColonyPlanner::plan() never checked the cap, so every 5s session re-planned a colony the host would refuse. Fix: refuse in plan() when planets->planetCount() >= getMaxPlanetAmount() (both host answers, gate 1). Verified live: players 12/17/20/26 now return null; ColonySpyExecutorTest 13/13.','2026-09-17 18:21:06'),
 (120,'RV-001','Solar satellite answers an energy shortfall the building queue cannot','impl','done','P2','P3 audit (piecepapercode-barakis)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/EnergyCapacity.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableBuildingPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableUnitPlanner.php','EnergyCapacity::pending() keeps only objects BuildingQueueObject::accepts(), so unit-based energy producers are unreachable and a planet in deficit whose affordable capacity buildings are exhausted falls through while its mines run at a fraction of their output. Run the same cheapest-first scan over the production objects the UNIT queue accepts, published as a unit intent. Seam: ObjectService::getGameObjectsWithProduction() with the unit accepts-check. Accept: frozen-clock case where an exhausted-deficit planet offers a solar-satellite intent while a planet that can still afford a plant offers the plant first; a mod-added energy unit needs no module edit. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 19:00:15'),
 (121,'RV-002','U6 launch subset: counter-select the launch per target and simulate before dispatch','impl','in_progress','P2','W6-4',NULL,'U5,U6','plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableUnitPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Infrastructure/Battle/NativeRaidEstimator.php','W6-4 shipped only the payload-sized cargo half. Production and launch are two decisions: the stock is what the account owns, the launch is the minimum hulls that win against THIS target. Derive the launch subset from the target-reported hull mix and defence using the host rapid-fire properties, simulate that subset once before dispatch, and let fodder ride only when the target can threaten the heavies. Accept: a light-fighter swarm draws cruisers, the same stock shown an undefended farm sends kill ships plus cargo, and a mod-added rapid-fire pair changes the selection with no module edit. Also the prerequisite for RV-007. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:53:49'),
 (122,'RV-003','Measure the defended-raid loot tier against the host own debris and repair values','review','todo','P2','W6-1',NULL,'T7','plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php; Modules/AI/plan/details/reviews/','RaidPlanner::LOOT_TIER_DEFENDED is a fixed 2.0 whose comment says debris subsidises a defended run, while claim RAID-014 decided debris stays out of the single-raid profit gate. One bounded read over existing artifacts (ai_decision_traces score components, ai_action_receipts, the estimator P20 output) asking whether the fixed tier admits a defended run the host debris and defence-repair values do not pay for, and whether it refuses one they do. Deliverable: a dated review record with the before figure and a verdict that either closes this as not-a-defect or points at RV-006. No code change. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:19'),
 (123,'RV-004','Mine production percentages as a real lever (throttle under deficit, restore after)','impl','todo','P2','P3 audit (ogame-opensource-2-ai)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Actions/SetAiMinePercentAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/EnergyCapacity.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableBuildingPlanner.php','The host lets a planet run each mine at a percentage (planets.*_percent via PlanetService::setBuildingPercent/getBuildingPercent, already exposed to players by ResourcesController) and the module uses neither side. One action and one rule: while the planet is in deficit, lower the mine with the worst output-per-energy to the highest percentage the remaining energy covers; when a capacity building lands, restore it. The object is chosen from host-reported production, never a machine name. Accept: frozen-clock case where exactly one mine is throttled, the host energy balance recovers, a later session restores it, and the receipt records before/after percentages. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:19'),
 (124,'RV-005','Confirm an admitted account owns a moon, and record its moon facilities','discovery','todo','P3','precondition gate',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md; Modules/AI/plan/details/reviews/','RV-008 and RV-009 cannot start without an owned moon and none exists today: the whole grand universe holds one moon (planets.planet_type = 3) and it is owned outside the cohort. Read planets for planet_type = 3 among admitted accounts, record which account owns one and which moon facilities it has, or record that none exists yet; a moon arrives through ordinary play (host calculateMoonChance on a fleet crash). Accept: a dated line naming the owner and its facilities, or stating none exists. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:19'),
 (125,'RV-006','Ground the defended loot tier in the host own debris and repair values','impl','todo','P2','W6-1',NULL,'T7','plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php','Applies the verdict RV-003 measured: replace the fixed LOOT_TIER_DEFENDED = 2.0 with the tier the host own debris and defence-repair values support, or close this row as not-a-defect if the measurement says the constant is right. No config knob. Accept: the frozen-clock raid tests stay green and a new test fails if a defended run is admitted at a tier the host debris/repair numbers do not cover. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:27'),
 (126,'RV-007','CRN screen-then-confirm ladder across launch subsets','impl','todo','P3','P3 audit (peterradzisz-fleet-optimizer)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Infrastructure/Battle/NativeRaidEstimator.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/RaidPlanner.php','One seed stream per candidate so two launch subsets are compared through common random numbers, a cheap screen over all candidates and the wide confirmation spent on the winner. Dead machinery before RV-002, because with fewer than two candidates the ladder has nothing to choose between - that is why it is gated. Accept: two subsets scored through the shared stream rank identically to a single-stream run, and the wide pass runs only on the winner (assert on the sample counter). Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:27'),
 (127,'RV-008','Sensor phalanx: build it on an owned moon, then scan the target before the raid','impl','todo','P3','P3 audit (alaingilbert-ogame)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueablePhalanxPlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/','PhalanxService ships in the host and the module never calls it. A fleeter with a moon scans before committing, and a scan is the only way to see a fleet stationed inside the planet that the espionage report cannot show. The row carries its own prerequisite: build the sensor phalanx on the moon first through the existing building path. Host canScanTarget is the only legality gate and must be respected exactly - an out-of-range scan is a ban risk, not a profit. One candidate source when a phalanx exists and the raid is otherwise viable, folded into the existing observation path. Accept: without a phalanx no scan candidate is published; with one the stationed fleet changes the raid decision; a host-refused scan is recorded and writes no game state. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:27'),
 (128,'RV-009','Jump gate: move the fleetsave between own moons instead of flying it','impl','todo','P3','P3 audit (janeczkins-xbot)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/QueueableFleetSavePlanner.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/QueueAiFleetSaveAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php','JumpGateService ships and is unused. With two owned moons a player moves the parked fleet between them instead of flying it - a save that costs no flight time - and the module fleetsave already ranks own bodies. Add the jump-gate move as one more destination kind the existing ranking can pick when it beats a flight, only when the cooldown and both facilities allow; the row carries building the gate as a FacilityChain step. Low value with a single moon: the mechanism is a destination pair. Accept: with one moon nothing changes; with two, a frozen-clock case picks the jump over the flight and a cooldown-blocked one falls back to the flight. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:27'),
 (129,'RV-010','Metal-dump research while saving (deferred on a measured case)','deferred','deferred','P3','P3 audit (trilogi77-ogamebot)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/FacilityChain.php; Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/EconomyUpgrades.php','TRIGGER: a measured metal-capped state that EconomyUpgrades::spendSurplus() and FacilityChain both leave unresolved - metal being discarded with an idle queue. The full-warehouse spend (W8-L4) and the facility chain already cover the ordinary case, and FacilityChain is the module only research source, so building this now is machinery for a value nothing varies on. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:34'),
 (130,'RV-011','Game-phase classification (deferred on a named consumer)','deferred','deferred','P3','P3 audit (shinigallo-ogame-agi)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Domain/Decision/; Modules/AI/plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','TRIGGER: a named consumer that varies a decision on the phase. The audit cut this for having no host seam, but a phase is derivable from host reads (own rank, object levels, the host highscore distribution) with no host change - so the missing piece is a consumer, not a seam. With none it is config for a value nothing varies on (gate 2). Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:34'),
 (131,'RV-012','Consultation confidence gate and horizon (deferred on the lane and a signal)','deferred','deferred','P3','P3 audit (shinigallo-ogame-agi)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/app/Actions/BuildCampaignConsultationBriefAction.php; Modules/AI/app/Actions/ApplyCampaignConsultationRankingAction.php','TRIGGER: the 6A/7A consultation lane enabled AND a confidence source present in the brief. The brief carries no confidence signal today and the lane is off by default, so suppressing a low-confidence nudge has nothing to suppress. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:34'),
 (132,'RV-013','Moonshot: sacrificial self-battle to farm debris (cut, not deferred)','deferred','deferred','P3','P3 audit (trilogi77-ogamebot)',NULL,NULL,'plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','Modules/AI/plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','CUT, recorded so it is not re-mined. AttackMission::checkOwnPlanet refuses self-attacks by design, so the self-battle seam does not exist; and sending a fleet to die on a neighbour to farm the debris is machine-shaped against gate 3 - no ordinary player does it. Reopens only if the owner asks for the host seam and a named-play justification. Doc: plan/details/specs/reopened-repo-value.md','2026-09-17 18:35:34'),
 (133,'W11-1','Ferry quote spent before dispatch — the transfer loop was refused by the host','impl','done','P1','W11-1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/Actions/QueueAiTransferAction.php; app/Domain/Decision/QueueableTransferPlanner.php; app/Enums/AiQueueActionReason.php','Closed 17 Sep 2026. Clamp the shipment to the source''s stock at dispatch, abandon a remnant below MINIMUM_SHIPMENT as source_short_at_dispatch, leave FleetMissionService::calculateConsumption fuel behind. Measured: 617/618 transfers refused in an hour before; 0 host resource refusals and 13 flown in the 90s after. 867 module tests green.','2026-09-17 18:38:02');
